# evidence-id|surface|encoding|payload
# Server-to-client lines for the client wire crate's server-direction decoder
# (ServerStreamFramer, parse_server_tags, parse_server_message), written by
# hand from Architecture Sections 7.4, 9.1, 9.2, 9.4, 9.5 and 10.3 and
# Appendix A.2, not produced by the renderer under test. The surface is
# accept/<name>, or reject/<stage>/<error>/<name> with the stage framing,
# tags or message and the error's variant. An ascii payload is one line and
# the reader appends its CRLF; a hex payload is the whole stream.
EVID-S02-008-RENDER|accept/welcome-001|ascii|:server.example 001 alice :Welcome to the ARC network alice
EVID-S02-008-RENDER|accept/myinfo-004|ascii|:server.example 004 alice server.example 1.0.0-rc.3 iw beIiklmnpst
EVID-S02-008-RENDER|accept/isupport-005|ascii|:server.example 005 alice AWAYLEN=256 CASEMAPPING=ascii CHANNELLEN=64 CHANTYPES=#& CHANMODES=beI,,kl,imnpst EXCEPTS=e INVEX=I KICKLEN=256 MAXLIST=b:100,e:100,I:100 MODES=6 :are supported by this server
EVID-S02-008-RENDER|accept/isupport-005-fifteen-parameters|ascii|:server.example 005 alice MONITOR=100 NICKLEN=32 PREFIX=(qaohv)~&@%+ SAFELIST STATUSMSG=@+ TARGMAX=PRIVMSG:4,NOTICE:4,TAGMSG:1,JOIN:20,PART:20 TOPICLEN=1024 UTF8ONLY EXTBAN=$,auncq LISTBUCKETS=1,2,5,10,25,50,100 NETWORK=ARC AGENCNET=AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA AWAYLEN=256 :are supported by this server
EVID-S02-008-RENDER|accept/server-ping|ascii|:server.example PING :AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA
EVID-S02-008-RENDER|accept/unprefixed-ping|ascii|PING :AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA
EVID-S02-008-RENDER|accept/user-privmsg|ascii|:alice!u-abcdefgh23@h-ijklmnopqrstuv67.invalid PRIVMSG #garden :hello: there
EVID-S02-008-RENDER|accept/extended-join|ascii|:alice!u-abcdefgh23@h-ijklmnopqrstuv67.invalid JOIN #garden heron :Alice
EVID-S02-008-RENDER|accept/account-900|ascii|:server.example 900 alice alice!u-abcdefgh23@h-ijklmnopqrstuv67.invalid heron :You are now logged in
